  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "PcUijjJnb7f/lG23Q7aJtwKp8yA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The one env var Connect's container still needs\n\nConnect's SPA never reads `process.env` at runtime \u2014 it fetches `/powerhouse.config.json`. That leaves an operator who runs the published image with no way to change branding, drives, renown or Sentry without rebuilding. `PH_CONNECT_CONFIG_JSON` closes that gap at the container boundary: the entrypoint deep-merges the payload into the **dist** `powerhouse.config.json` at container start, which is exactly equivalent to pre-running `ph connect config --json '{...}'` against that file. The SPA then reads the file as usual.\n\n### Operator-wins semantics\n\n- A **concrete value** in the payload overwrites whatever was baked or mounted.\n- A **`null` leaf**, or an omitted key, keeps the file's existing value.\n- **`connect.app.basePath` is ignored.** The base path is baked into the bundled asset URLs at build time \u2014 rebuild with `--base`, or build once with `--dynamic-base` to resolve it at serve time.\n\n```bash\ndocker run -e PH_CONNECT_CONFIG_JSON='{\n  \"connect\": {\n    \"app\": { \"logLevel\": \"debug\" },\n    \"renown\": { \"url\": \"https://renown.staging.example\", \"chainId\": 137 },\n    \"drives\": { \"sections\": { \"remote\": { \"enabled\": true, \"allowAdd\": false } } },\n    \"sentry\": { \"dsn\": \"https://prod-key@sentry.io/1\", \"env\": \"prod\", \"tracing\": true }\n  }\n}' connect:latest\n```\n\nThe accepted shape is the same one `ph connect config --json` takes, schema'd at `packages/builder-tools/connect-utils/runtime-config.schema.json`.\n\n### Fails loudly, not silently\n\nMalformed JSON or a non-object payload **aborts container startup** with a stderr message rather than dropping the operator's intent and booting with stale config. That is deliberate: a silently-ignored payload in production is far worse than a crash-loop you can see.\n\nThis is the migration target for the retired per-field variables \u2014 `PH_CONNECT_LOG_LEVEL`, `PH_CONNECT_DISABLE_ADD_DRIVE`, `PH_CONNECT_RENOWN_URL`, `PH_CONNECT_DEFAULT_DRIVES_URL`, the whole `PH_CONNECT_SENTRY_*` family. Wrap their values into one payload. The Sentry *release* tag stays build-time only: it is stamped into the bundle from `WORKSPACE_VERSION` so it always matches CI's sourcemap upload.\n\n_Source: `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/05-Launch/05-DockerDeployment.md`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z"
    }
  },
